# Python bytecode. Running the mandated leak-check ritual generates these,
# and without this file a `git add -A` sweeps them into the commit — which
# is exactly how tools/__pycache__/leak_check.cpython-311.pyc ended up
# tracked in PR #6.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Build artifacts from the packaging ritual
*.zip
build/
dist/
# npm pack output. `npm pack` (without --dry-run) drops a tarball in the
# package dir; it is a build artifact and must never be committed.
*.tgz

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Agent worktrees and local session scratch. Claude Code creates
# .claude/worktrees/agent-*/ containing full working copies of this repo,
# including MAINTAINERS.md and everything under tools/. Untracked AND
# unignored, they sat one `git add -A` away from committing a duplicate tree
# to a public repo. They also broke the admin surface census, which enumerates
# with `ls-files --others`: it failed on a developer machine and passed in a
# clean container, so the committed map was reproducible by neither.
.claude/
